    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Écrire le -ing",
     "md": "- On ajoute **-ing** : *play → playing, eat → eating*.\n- Verbe en **-e** : on enlève le e : *make → making*.\n- Petit verbe avec une voyelle + une consonne : on double la consonne : *run → running, sit → sitting*."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Mots qui aident",
     "md": "On trouve souvent : **now**, **at the moment**, **today**, **look!**, **listen!**\n\n- Négation : *I am not playing. She isn't playing.*\n- Question : *Are you eating? Is he sleeping?*"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 1 : compléter",
     "statement": "Complète : « Look ! Mballa (run) in the yard. »",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "« Look ! » annonce une action **en ce moment**."
      },
      {
       "md": "Sujet Mballa = he → **is**."
      },
      {
       "md": "run → **running** (on double le n) : *Mballa is running in the yard.*"
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**Mballa is running in the yard.**"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 2 : habitude ou maintenant ?",
     "statement": "Choisis : « Every day I (walk / am walking) to school. Now I (walk / am walking) in the rain. »",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "« Every day » → habitude → **present simple** : walk."
      },
      {
       "md": "« Now » → action en cours → **present continuous** : am walking."
      },
      {
       "md": "La phrase : *Every day I walk to school. Now I am walking in the rain.*"
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**Every day I walk… Now I am walking…**"
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Erreurs fréquentes",
     "md": "- Oublier am / is / are : *She reading* est faux → *She is reading*.\n- Oublier le -ing : *He is play* est faux → *He is playing*.\n- Garder le e : *making*, pas *makeing*."
    },
